  "full_text": "I got an idea for government. There's a story, a joke, about a lighthouse and a... Oh, fucked it up. Fuck! Okay, so, this Navy lieutenant gets on the radio and says, ship bearing so-and-so, change course, 10 degrees to your right, port, left, or starboard. The voice on the radio comes back, cannot comply. And then the voice says again, change course. I'm an aircraft carrier and I'm a lieutenant in the Navy or whatever the fuck it is. Admiral, no, whatever. One of them things. Anyway, so I'm a radio operator in the Navy. And he says, no, cannot comply. And then he says, hello, this is. Admiral, or no, I don't know, he probably wouldn't put the Admiral on there. But the radio says, I am on board USS Ronald Reagan, and I have a whole carrier fleet. Change course immediately. And he says, look, dude, I'm just a lighthouse operator. Your decision, right? So Mr. Terry's got the voice of God coming down. So I can just say this shit, and this is your decision, you know? We can run the government that way. I have absolute authority as a goddamn lighthouse operator, okay? I don't need any fucking authority other than the authority of a goddamn lighthouse operator. So there you go.",
